und antecedent (counter equal to 2 with req high)"}], "files": [{"path": "rr_arbiter.sby", "kind": "formal_spec", "title": "SymbiYosys job for rr_arbiter (single task, prove mode, depth 20)", "summary": "Single-task SymbiYosys job with no [tasks] section. It uses mode prove with the smtbmc engine at depth 20; prove mode is k-induction, so a pass means an unbounded proof, not only a bounded check. It reads the approved RTL rr_arbiter.v [artifact:prj-238bc15062.design-under-test.a1] by its own name, reads rr_arbiter_props.sv, and lists both under [files]. Top module: rr_arbiter_formal. Depth 20 is meant to leave enough cycles for every cover to be reached [requirement:req-2e425ae6da].", "entry": "rr_arbiter_formal"}, {"path": "rr_arbiter_props.sv", "kind": "assertions", "title": "Formal wrapper and properties for rr_arbiter", "summary": "Wrapper module rr_arbiter_formal. It instantiates rr_arbiter from [artifact:prj-238bc15062.design-under-test.a1] and holds immediate assertions, assumptions and covers in Yosys read -formal style. They trace to the RR-RESET, RR-IDLE, RR-PICK, RR-ONLY-REQUESTERS, RR-ROTATE, RR-HOLD, RR-YIELD and RR-BOUND items of [artifact:prj-238bc15062.interface-spec.a1].", "entry": "rr_arbiter_formal"}], "tool_runs": [], "claims": ["By hand-tracing the RTL against the spec I expect all assertions to hold and all covers to be reachable within 20 cycles. This is a manual analysis only, not a tool result.", "RR-BOUND is checked only over reset-free intervals; the wait counters clear on reset. A mid-run reset sets last to 2 and can extend a wait beyond three edges. I read the spec's bound as applying between resets.", "Before the first reset edge, last is unconstrained and may be 3. Combinational checks are therefore gated on f_past_valid, meaning at least one reset edge has occurred."], "escalation": null, "notes": "Interpretation to confirm in review: RR-BOUND excludes intervals that contain a reset. The spec does not say so explicitly; the RTL reload